    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2021-november/q1",
      "question": "<p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is an enlargement, centre the origin, with scale factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k&gt;0\"></span></p><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> is a rotation through angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> degrees anticlockwise about the origin.</p><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> followed by the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> is represented by the matrix</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M=\\begin{pmatrix}-4&amp;-4\\sqrt3\\\\4\\sqrt3&amp;-4\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Determine<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>,</li><li>the smallest value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol></li></ol><p>A square <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span> has vertices at the points with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(a, -a)\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2a, 0)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(a, a)\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>The square <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span> is transformed to the square <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S^{\\prime}\"></span> by the transformation represented by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Determine, in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S^{\\prime}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
