    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2021-november/q3",
      "question": "<p>The cubic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"ax^3+bx^2-19x-b=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants, has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\gamma\"></span></p><p>The cubic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"w^3-9w^2-97w+c=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> is a constant, has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4\\alpha-1)\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4\\beta-1)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4\\gamma-1)\"></span></p><p>Without solving either cubic equation, determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
