      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2021-november/q5",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Evaluate the improper integral<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_1^{\\infty}2\\mathrm e^{-\\frac12 x}\\,\\mathrm dx\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>The air temperature, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span>, on a particular day in London is modelled by the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\theta=8-5\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}t\\right)-\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}t\\right)\\qquad 0\\leqslant t\\leqslant 24\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is the number of hours after midnight.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Use calculus to show that the mean air temperature on this day is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span>, according to the model. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the actual mean air temperature recorded on this day was higher than <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>explain how the model could be refined. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol></li></ol>",
