    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2021-november/q6",
      "question": "<p>A tourist decides to do a bungee jump from a bridge over a river.<br>One end of an elastic rope is attached to the bridge and the other end of the elastic rope is attached to the tourist.<br>The tourist jumps off the bridge.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds after the tourist reaches their lowest point, their vertical displacement is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> metres above a fixed point 30 metres vertically above the river.</p><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\"></span></p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-20\"></span></li><li>the velocity of the tourist is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span></li><li>the acceleration of the tourist is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"13.6\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}\"></span></li></ul><p>In the subsequent motion, the elastic rope is assumed to remain taut so that the vertical displacement of the tourist can be modelled by the differential equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5k\\frac{\\mathrm d^2x}{\\mathrm dt^2}+2k\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}+17x=0\\qquad t\\geqslant 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a positive constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Determine the particular solution to the differential equation. <span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li><li>Hence find, according to the model, the vertical height of the tourist above the river 15 seconds after they have reached their lowest point. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Give a limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
